        "paragraphs": [
            "StepFun Step is a family of models from the developer StepFun, offered through the StepFun Open Platform. StepFun says the family includes a new-generation frontier model built for real-world tasks, the flagship model for agentic work, high-speed multimodal reasoning models, high-speed models for agent and coding tasks, and a version optimized for high-frequency agent scenarios. The family also covers speech and smart routing, with models for contextual text to speech, automatic speech recognition, and a smart routing model that dispatches requests by task complexity. StepFun says more flagship models will be added over time.",
            "The models are available through Step Plan, a subscription service from the StepFun API Platform that lets you use StepFun models at a subscription price in coding tools and agent platforms such as OpenClaw, Claude Code, Trae, and Cursor. Step Plan uses Credits as its unified billing unit and offers four tiers, Flash Mini, Flash Plus, Flash Pro, and Flash Max, which differ in monthly Credit allowance and price. StepFun also offers Step Code, a terminal AI agent for software development and everyday terminal tasks, built by StepFun and optimized for Step models. StepFun says Step Code reads and edits code, executes shell commands, searches files, fetches web pages, and plans its next steps based on execution feedback."
        ],
